# A raise in each callback the cask keeps for its host (decision 096 of
# note/project/term/self-host/change/001-finish-self-host): the app writes no guard, the program builds on Rust, and
# test/call/update-rust.ts runs both tasks to see the library report each raise and the program go on. `check-raising`
# meets the real update client. `wired` needs a window, so that test runs it over a stand-in for the shim's stub half
# that calls each kept closure at once.

load @term/cask/cask
  find window
  find on-message
  find on-ready
  find on-close
  find snapshot
  find update-check

task check-raising
  take resources, like text
  take data, like text
  take base, like text
  call update-check
    read resources
    read data
    read base
    text <main>
    task heard
      take status, like text
      like void
      halt <no status {status}>

task wired
  take made, like window
  take shot, like text
  call on-message
    read made
    task answer
      mark async
      take message, like text
      like text
      halt <no answer {message}>
  call on-ready
    read made
    task drawn
      like void
      halt <not drawn>
  call snapshot
    read made
    read shot
    task done
      like void
      halt <not shot>
  call on-close
    read made
    task closed
      like void
      halt <not closed>
